% ============================================================================
% mitosis-phases.query.adj — a worked recall over the biology mitosis library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what happens in
% metaphase?": it states no biology fact — it only `import`s the grounded table
% and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `mitosis_phase` rows and returns the event atom + the table's
% source/locator/trust. The fifth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the
% event, recall the phase). A word that is not one of the four mitotic phases —
% `interphase`, the resting stage BETWEEN divisions — abstains honestly: the
% engine never invents an event.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli mitosis-phases.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "mitosis-phases.adj"

? mitosis_phase(prophase, $E)    % expect chromatin_forms_chromosomes
? mitosis_phase(metaphase, $E)   % expect chromosomes_line_up
? mitosis_phase(anaphase, $E)    % expect chromatids_separate
? mitosis_phase(telophase, $E)   % expect nuclear_membrane_forms
? mitosis_phase($P, chromosomes_line_up)  % expect metaphase — the reverse recall
? mitosis_phase(interphase, $E)  % expect abstain — not a phase OF mitosis
